{"id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op.1","title":"Nonce slice copy panics if KDF returns wrong length","description":"File: oscore/src/edhoc/initiator.rs:442-443

Issue: `nonce.copy_from_slice(&iv_3)` will panic if `iv_3.len() != NONCE_LEN` (13 bytes). While `edhoc_kdf` is called with `NONCE_LEN` as the requested length, there is no assertion that the returned vector actually has that length before the copy.

Trigger: If `edhoc_kdf` were to return a shorter vector (e.g., due to internal buffer constraints or HKDF implementation quirk), the `copy_from_slice` would panic with an unhelpful error.

Suggested fix: Add length assertion or use `try_into()`:
```rust
let iv_3: [u8; NONCE_LEN] = iv_3.as_slice().try_into()
    .map_err(|_| EdhocError::KeyDerivation)?;
nonce.copy_from_slice(&iv_3);
```","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"me@mark.atwood.name","created_at":"2026-08-16T18:41:27.348659Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-08-16T18:41:27.348659Z","labels":["correctness","edge-case","review"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op.1","depends_on_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-x6op","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-08-16T18:41:27.756763Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}
